John hires a reliable driving service to get him to work each day. His work is 30 miles away and he has to go there and back each day. He goes to work 5 days a week for 50 weeks a year. He gets charged $2 per mile driven and he also gives his driver a $150 bonus per month. How much does he pay a year for driving?,John hires a driving service to get him to work each day. His work is 30 miles away and he has to go there and back each day. He goes to work 5 days a week for 50 weeks a year. He gets charged $2 per mile driven and he also gives his driver a $150 bonus per month. How much does he pay a year for driving?,31800,31800,318,318,"Let's solve this step by step:

### Step 1: Calculate the total miles driven per day.
John's work is 30 miles away, and he has to go there and back each day.  
So, the total miles driven per day is:  
\[
30 \, \text{miles (one way)} \times 2 = 60 \, \text{miles per day}.
\]

### Step 2: Calculate the total miles driven per week.
John goes to work 5 days a week.  
The total miles driven per week is:  
\[
60 \, \text{miles per day} \times 5 \, \text{days per week} = 300 \, \text{miles per week}.
\]

### Step 3: Calculate the total miles driven per year.
John works 50 weeks a year.  
The total miles driven per year is:  
\[
300 \, \text{miles per week} \times 50 \, \text{weeks per year} = 15,000 \, \text{miles per year}.
\]

### Step 4: Calculate the cost of driving based on mileage.
John is charged $2 per mile driven.  
The total cost for mileage is:  
\[
15,000 \, \text{miles per year} \times 2 \, \text{dollars per mile} = 30,000 \, \text{dollars}.
\]

### Step 5: Calculate the total bonus paid per year.
John gives his driver a $150 bonus per month. There are 12 months in a year.  
The total bonus paid per year is:  
\[
150 \, \text{dollars per month} \times 12 \, \text{months per year} = 1,800 \, \text{dollars}.
\]

### Step 6: Calculate the total amount John pays per year.
The total cost for driving is the sum of the mileage cost and the bonus:  
\[
30,000 \, \text{dollars (mileage cost)} + 1,800 \, \text{dollars (bonus)} = 31,800 \, \text{dollars}.
\]

